# Changelog (engine/v1/)

## CONFIG values are raw numbers

**What:** Every spatial value in `API_CONFIG` (`ENGINE.Config`) is now a plain number with its unit named in a comment: `Debug.Levels.BoundingBox.Grid.Size` (CNU), `Physics.Gravity.Strength` (CNU/s²), `Physics.Gravity.TerminalVelocity.Air/Water` (CNU/s), `Physics.Buoyancy.Force.Min/Max` (CNU/s²), `Physics.Buoyancy.GradientDepth` (CNU), `Camera.ZoomStep` (CNU). `Camera.Fov` and `Physics.Correction.MaxAngleDelta` are labelled degrees. Engine reads drop `.value`; the debug grid converts with `CNUtoWorldUnit`. Forces.js drag coefficients are now functions that read CONFIG live, not import-time constants. The engine-only exports in config.js stay Unit-instanced. UNIT_INSTANCING.md gained a §1 "Exception: CONFIG".

**Where:** [config.js](engine/v1/core/config.js), [Forces.js](engine/v1/math/Forces.js), [physics/Master.js](engine/v1/physics/Master.js), [Correction.js](engine/v1/physics/Correction.js), [Modes.js](engine/v1/camera/Modes.js), [Render.js](engine/v1/handlers/Render.js), [Level.js](engine/v1/handlers/game/Level.js), [UNIT_INSTANCING.md](engine/v1/docs/rules/UNIT_INSTANCING.md)

## Camera mode angles are Units

**What:** orbitCam's `yaw`/`pitch` and freeCam's persisted view `yaw`/`pitch` are degree Units; chaseCam/sideCam's `side`/`settle` are radian Units. A reusable `chaseRuntime.look` holds the chase frame's look as degree Units. `consumeLookInput` writes `.value` on the view's Unit yaw and pitch, and readers convert with `.toRadians()`/`.toDegrees()`.

**Where:** [Modes.js](engine/v1/camera/Modes.js)

## Camera and movement angles passed between functions are Units

**What:** In camera modes, `settlePitch`, `armPitch`, `chasePitch`, `gapToTrail` and `stiffen` return radian Units. `pitchWindow` takes a Unit settle and returns degree-Unit `top`/`bottom`/`min`/`max`. `chaseFreedom` returns those plus a radian-Unit `yaw`; its `minPitch`/`maxPitch` fields became `min`/`max`. `consumeLookInput` takes Unit pitch bounds, and `armAt`/`armBasis` take Unit angles. `wrapDegrees` wraps a degree Unit in place, and a read-only `noTurn` zero-radian Unit was added. `modeData.yaw` from freeCam and orbitCam is a radian Unit. The player input frame's `previousCameraYaw` and `lockAngle` are radian Units; `advanceCarriedForward` and `lockedDirection` take Unit angles. `cameraState.fov` was removed: the projection matrix and loop framing read `CONFIG.Camera.Fov` directly.

**Where:** [Modes.js](engine/v1/camera/Modes.js), [camera/Master.js](engine/v1/camera/Master.js), [Movement.js](engine/v1/player/Movement.js), [NewEntity.js](engine/v1/builder/NewEntity.js), [Render.js](engine/v1/handlers/Render.js)

## Spatial rates are instanced

**What:** Character meta `maxSpeed` (CNU/s), `acceleration`/`deceleration` (CNU/s²) and `momentumTurnRate` are now Units, instanced next to `jumpHeight`. `momentumTurnRate` is authored in degrees/s (14 rad/s → 802.14 on all four characters) and converted with `.toRadians(true)`. `level.player.metaOverrides` instances the same keys plus `jumpHeight`, now taken as a plain number instead of `{ value }`. The default model turn rate is `new Unit(458.37, "degrees").toRadians(true)`, cloned into each entity's `modelTurnRate`; the player scales it into radian Units. `turnFacingToward` and `stepModelRotation` take a Unit max step. `CONFIG.Physics.Correction.ReferenceReleaseRate` is 229.18 degrees/s (was 4 rad/s), converted where it's used. The camera loop tracker's `turned`/`arcTurn` (radians) and `arc`/`radius` (CNU) are Units. `PlayerHeight` returns a CNU Unit, and `sceneGraph.loopSurfaces` radii are CNU Units. Already-instanced velocities and speeds are labelled per second where they're instanced. UNIT_INSTANCING.md gained a §1 "Rates" subsection.

**Where:** [characters.json](engine/v1/player/characters.json), [Instance.js](engine/v1/builder/templates/Instance.js), [normalize.js](engine/v1/core/normalize.js), [Movement.js](engine/v1/player/Movement.js), [player/Master.js](engine/v1/player/Master.js), [Model.js](engine/v1/player/Model.js), [NewEntity.js](engine/v1/builder/NewEntity.js), [NewLevel.js](engine/v1/builder/NewLevel.js), [NewParticles.js](engine/v1/builder/NewParticles.js), [Animation.js](engine/v1/handlers/game/Animation.js), [physics/Collision.js](engine/v1/physics/Collision.js), [Correction.js](engine/v1/physics/Correction.js), [config.js](engine/v1/core/config.js), [camera/Master.js](engine/v1/camera/Master.js), [Modes.js](engine/v1/camera/Modes.js), [UNIT_INSTANCING.md](engine/v1/docs/rules/UNIT_INSTANCING.md)

## Unit and UnitVector3 are engine-exclusive

**What:** `ENGINE.Math.Instancing` (`Unit`, `UnitVector3`) was removed from the game API, along with the now-unused import in ini.js. MODULE_GROUPS §3 and UNIT_INSTANCING §1 now state that `Unit`/`UnitVector3` are engine-exclusive: games never receive them, and math/ never uses them.

**Where:** [ini.js](engine/v1/core/ini.js), [MODULE_GROUPS.md](engine/v1/docs/rules/MODULE_GROUPS.md), [UNIT_INSTANCING.md](engine/v1/docs/rules/UNIT_INSTANCING.md)

## Game-exposed force math takes a plain water level

**What:** `ComputeBuoyancy`, `ComputeSubmergence` and `ComputeStepVelocity`'s buoyancy input take `waterLevel` as a plain CNU number or null instead of a Unit. physics/Forces.js unwraps the scene's water-level Unit through a new `waterLevelOf`, which passes null through. Movement's buoyancy step-sim passes `waterLevel: 0`.

**Where:** [math/Forces.js](engine/v1/math/Forces.js), [physics/Forces.js](engine/v1/physics/Forces.js), [Movement.js](engine/v1/player/Movement.js)

## Shared CloneTransform and Unit.math

**What:** `Unit.math(f, ...args)` sets the value to `f(value, ...args)` and returns the Unit. It is used for the camera's obstruction distance smoothing and the player's jump apex tracking. `CloneTransform` (math/Utilities.js, exposed as `ENGINE.Math.Other.CloneTransform`) copies a transform. Instanced position, rotation and pivot are cloned as UnitVector3, plain ones are copied as plain vectors, scale is always copied, and pivot is copied only if present. It replaces NewEntity.js `cloneRootTransform`/`cloneLocalTransform`, and the inline copies in Matrix.js `CreateRenderMatrixCache` and Animation.js `buildModelPose`/`applyPartLocal`. `applyModelPose` builds `model.posedTransform` directly with it. Scale is now copied where it used to be shared with the source. UNIT_INSTANCING.md gained a §3 exception for `CloneTransform`'s `instanceof` check and a §7 `.math` pattern.

**Where:** [Utilities.js](engine/v1/math/Utilities.js), [Matrix.js](engine/v1/math/Matrix.js), [NewEntity.js](engine/v1/builder/NewEntity.js), [Animation.js](engine/v1/handlers/game/Animation.js), [camera/Master.js](engine/v1/camera/Master.js), [player/Master.js](engine/v1/player/Master.js), [ini.js](engine/v1/core/ini.js), [UNIT_INSTANCING.md](engine/v1/docs/rules/UNIT_INSTANCING.md)

## Capsule colliders reach full height again

**What:** `CapsuleFromAabb` clones `segmentEnd` from the box center before `segmentStart` shifts down, so the segment spans the full box height instead of ending at the center.

**Where:** [math/Collision.js](engine/v1/math/Collision.js)

## Animated decals on flat faces are no longer cut to their rest footprint

**What:** `flatDecalFacets` grows the flat decal quad (positions and UVs) by the decal's animation margin, the same margin curved hosts already use. `decalAnimationMargin` also accounts for spin, adding √2 when any keyframe rotates the decal.

**Where:** [Render.js](engine/v1/handlers/Render.js)

## Overlap push uses the shallower of collider and box depth

**What:** `DetectCurrentPhysicsOverlaps` measures how far the entity's AABB and the candidate's AABB overlap along the contact normal. It pushes the entity out by whichever is smaller: that box overlap or the collider's contact depth. The candidate AABB is looked up once and reused for both the overlap gate and the depth.

**Where:** [physics/Collision.js](engine/v1/physics/Collision.js)

## Grounded model turns at the full rate

**What:** Entities have a `modelTurnRate.ground` rate, the default 450°/s with no scaling; the player reuses the base entity's. `resolveModelPose` uses the water rate when underwater, the ground rate when grounded, and the air rate otherwise.

**Where:** [NewEntity.js](engine/v1/builder/NewEntity.js), [player/Master.js](engine/v1/player/Master.js), [Animation.js](engine/v1/handlers/game/Animation.js)

## Player model turns at the full rate out of water

**What:** The player's `modelTurnRate.air` (out of water) is the base rate with no `airControl` scaling. `water` still scales by `underwaterAirControl`. The `modelTurnRate.ground` key from the previous entry is removed again, and `resolveModelPose` uses water when underwater and air otherwise.

**Where:** [player/Master.js](engine/v1/player/Master.js), [NewEntity.js](engine/v1/builder/NewEntity.js), [Animation.js](engine/v1/handlers/game/Animation.js)

## Dead face-remapping code removed from entity parts

**What:** Removed `remapRotatedFaces`, the `faceMap` part field and its writes in `buildModel`, and the unused `builtPosition`/`builtRotation`/`builtScale` part fields. `builtDimensions` stays. The `BestMatchOf` import is dropped.

**Where:** [NewEntity.js](engine/v1/builder/NewEntity.js)

## Entity bounds scaling and rest-pose save use shared helpers

**What:** `computeScaledBounds` scales sphere, capsule and compound-sphere radii (and the capsule half-height) with `scaleUnit`. `captureRestCollision` saves the root transform with one `CloneTransform` call.

**Where:** [NewEntity.js](engine/v1/builder/NewEntity.js)

## Loop-surface detection split out of surface chunking

**What:** Loop-surface detection moved from `buildSurfaceChunks` into a new `findLoopSurfaces(pieces, owner, facets, links)`, which also computes the per-facet incline. `buildSurfaceChunks` builds pieces, links and chunks, then calls it. Its `{ chunks, loopSurfaces }` return is unchanged.

**Where:** [NewLevel.js](engine/v1/builder/NewLevel.js)

## Chase camera's post-loop return works again

**What:** `PrepareCamera` reads `cameraState.looping` into `wasLooping` before the situation updates, and sets `frame.leftLoop = wasLooping && !cameraState.looping`. `leftLoop` is true again on the frame a loop situation ends, so `prepareChase` starts its return.

**Where:** [camera/Master.js](engine/v1/camera/Master.js)

## "last" prefix for state from before

**What:** Names holding earlier state now use `last`:
- `loop.lastUp`/`lastPosition`, `frame.lastMode` (was `from`) and `lastLooping` in the camera.
- orbitCam's `lastDirection`, and chase's `lastPitch`/`pitch` (was `pitch`/`nextPitch`).
- The entity input frame's `lastCameraYaw`/`lastHasInput`/`lastGrounded`/`lastUp`/`lastKeys`/`lastControl`.
- `physicsRuntime.lastPosition`/`lastRotation`, and physics' `lastGrounded`.
- `playerState.lastAction`.
- `hasMeaningfulVectorDelta(vector, corrected)`.
- `MeasureRefreshRate`'s `lastTime`.

The player action event's `from`/`to` keys are unchanged. ENGINE_SEMANTICS gained §6 "Last and Next". The old §6 is now §7.

**Where:** [camera/Master.js](engine/v1/camera/Master.js), [Modes.js](engine/v1/camera/Modes.js), [NewEntity.js](engine/v1/builder/NewEntity.js), [Movement.js](engine/v1/player/Movement.js), [player/Master.js](engine/v1/player/Master.js), [physics/Master.js](engine/v1/physics/Master.js), [Correction.js](engine/v1/physics/Correction.js), [Performance.js](engine/v1/handlers/game/Performance.js), [ENGINE_SEMANTICS.md](engine/v1/docs/rules/ENGINE_SEMANTICS.md)

## Past-tense booleans and the action event's keys

**What:** Booleans that hold whether something was true now use the past tense:
- `wasLooping` in `PrepareCamera` and `wasGrounded` in physics, replacing `lastLooping`/`lastGrounded`.
- The entity input frame's `wasGrounded` and `hadInput`, replacing `lastGrounded`/`lastHasInput`.

The `PLAYER_ACTION_CHANGE` payload's `from`/`to` keys are now `lastAction`/`action`, and `SetPlayerAction` takes `action`.

ENGINE_SEMANTICS §6 now covers the was/had form for booleans and limits `next` to deliberate use: the next item in a sequence, or a value calculated ahead.

**Where:** [camera/Master.js](engine/v1/camera/Master.js), [physics/Master.js](engine/v1/physics/Master.js), [NewEntity.js](engine/v1/builder/NewEntity.js), [Movement.js](engine/v1/player/Movement.js), [player/Master.js](engine/v1/player/Master.js), [ENGINE_SEMANTICS.md](engine/v1/docs/rules/ENGINE_SEMANTICS.md)
